### Step 4 — Write eval_result.json

Write the following JSON to `{{ WORKDIR }}/eval_result.json` (fill in your scores):

> **CRITICAL FORMAT CONSTRAINT**: The JSON MUST be a **flat object** — all fields at the root level, NO nesting under "evaluation", "result", "scores" or any other parent key. Use EXACTLY the field names shown below. The scoring pipeline reads `score_ratio` directly from the root; nested structures will cause parsing failure.

```json
{
  "task_type": "development",
  "eval_mode": "gold",
  "static_score": <STATIC_SCORE>,
  "static_reason": "<STATIC_REASON>",
  "dynamic_score": <DYNAMIC_SCORE or null>,
  "dynamic_reason": "<DYNAMIC_REASON>",
  "total_score": <TOTAL_SCORE>,
  "max_score": <MAX_SCORE>,
  "score_ratio": <SCORE_RATIO>,
  "notes": "<NOTES>"
}
```

> **PROHIBITED patterns** (will cause parsing failure and score = 0):
> ```
> ❌ WRONG — nested structure:
>    { "evaluation": { "static_score": 1, ... } }
>    { "result": { "score_ratio": 0.75 } }
>    { "scores": { "static_score": 1, "dynamic_score": 2 } }
> ❌ WRONG — missing score_ratio:
>    { "static_score": 1, "dynamic_score": 2, "total_score": 3 }
> ✅ CORRECT — flat object with ALL required fields including score_ratio:
>    { "task_type": "development", "eval_mode": "gold", "static_score": 1, ..., "score_ratio": 0.75 }
> ```

